//! name: adaptor-chain-rigid-receiver-accepted
//! rule: 09.R43
//! expect: check-ok
//! detail: R43 -- for a rigid receiver the candidate traits are exactly its bounds, so `I: Iterator` finds `map`; the generic item is instantiated (`same[I.Item]`, R28), and the result is `Mapped[I, I.Item]` with `I.Item: Droppable` from the trait's bound

needs { };

fn same[T](sink x: T) -> T { return x; }

fn f[I: Iterator](sink it: I) -> usize {
    return it.map(same[I.Item]).count();
}
